//? Title: SRT division: redundant digits and actual partial remainders
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A radix-two redundant quotient uses digits -1,0,+1 to keep the partial remainder
bounded. This floating simulation exposes the actual selector, normalization and
accumulator rather than a separately replayed remainder curve.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Normalize d into[1/2,1) and scale n by the same power of two. Starting P0=n, at
digit j set w=2P, choose +1 at w>=1/2, -1 at w<=-1/2 and0 otherwise, then
P=w-q*d. Accumulate Qj=sum(q_i*2^-i). In exact arithmetic n/d=Qj+Pj/(d*2^j),
and |Pj|<d yields error<2^-j. This mathematical tail is distinct from double
rounding and underflow. The selector uses complete floating values; it is not a
hardware leading-bit lookup or timing model.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/srt_division_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::srt_division_trace(.7, .9, 8);
    std::print("| digit | remainder before | shifted | q | remainder after | prefix |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} |\n", s.index,
                   s.before, s.shifted, s.digit, s.after, s.value);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("Normalized divisor {:.4g}",
                                     r.normalized_divisor));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual redundant digits",
                                     r.digits.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual prefix {:.7g}", r.value));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/srt_division_tiny.svg");
}
```
