> API and interpretation

Finite proper fractions0<=N<D with positive D are supported. Negative/oversized
counts and invalid operands fail explicitly. The nominal tail is an
exact-arithmetic reference represented as double, not a certificate for the
floating result. Extremely small normalized numerators or long-digit weights can
underflow. Histories and legacy digit reconstruction share the same producer
accumulator.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

